# Every text file is stored with LF in the repo, whatever the contributor's OS.
# Without this, a Windows commit can rewrite every line ending of a file and the
# pull request shows the whole file as changed, which also breeds merge
# conflicts. It also keeps shell scripts runnable inside the Linux container.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Test fixtures are compared byte for byte against their manifest, so git must
# never rewrite their line endings on checkout: with core.autocrlf=true a Windows
# clone turned a 902-line HTML capture into 902 extra bytes and failed
# tests/unit/test_employer_website_rung.py::test_captured_pages_match_their_manifest.
# This rule must stay below the one above: the later match wins.
tests/fixtures/** -text
